    "note": "Public Chapter 606, approved 2026-03-27, effective July 1, 2026 (leases entered, amended, extended or renewed on or after Jan 1, 2027 per summary). Chaptered copy names SB 350 (substituted for HB 469). Landlords may require concealed, holstered or contained carry in common areas (subsection (b)); exemptions in (c) not quoted. Quote spacing 'subdivision(a)(1)' is as printed."
  },
  "operative_text": "SECTION 1 (new TCA 66-7-113(a)): (a) A landlord shall not prohibit lawful possession, carrying, transportation, or storage of a firearm, any part of a firearm, or firearm ammunition by a residential tenant: (1) Within the residential tenant's leased residential premises; (2) In a vehicle located in the parking area provided for residential tenants by the landlord of the leased residential premises; or (3) Except as provided in subsection (b), in other locations controlled by the landlord, but only to the extent necessary to directly enter or exit the locations described in subdivision(a)(1) or (a)(2).\nSECTION 1 (new TCA 66-7-113(d)): (d) A tenant who is adversely affected by a violation of subsection (a) may bring a suit against the landlord for declaratory and injunctive relief, actual damages, punitive damages, and recovery of attorney fees.\nSECTION 2 (new TCA 66-28-206(a)): (a) A landlord shall not prohibit lawful possession, carrying, transportation, or storage of a firearm, any part of a firearm, or firearm ammunition by a tenant: (1) Within the tenant's dwelling unit; (2) In a vehicle located in the parking area provided for tenants by the landlord of the dwelling unit; or (3) Except as provided in subsection (b), in other locations controlled by the landlord, but only to the extent necessary to directly enter or exit the locations described in subdivision (a)(1) and (a)(2)."
